Ranger -- Neutral human.

2nd best game I've ever had. Didn't finish quest yet, but I was 
basically
going up and down the levels to gain ~10000 more exp points. (well,
mistake kinda. I should have had less pets, and done more fighting)
My protection run and vaults were nearly complete (might as well do
that) so I was ~3 naked AC. My armor wasn't that good, but -10 seems
fine for pre-quest. Killed Medusa, didn't clear the castle, but I 
didn't
feel like I "needed" the wish so much. So I wanted a my Quest 
Artifact
(Longbow of Diana) so that I could shoot arrows at the eels and 
sharks
while doing the guillotine movement.

This is also the first game I've ever had teleport control. Its so 
risky
to get. This is also one of the first games where I had more than 
18/75
strength, and at this point, nearly all my stats were maxed out.

So what happened?

I stepped on a level-teleport trap. On purpose, of course. I felt that
I was wasting time and should just clear the castle. THEN do the
quest.

So I step on the level teleporter. The castle was about 25 or so 
stories
down, so...

What level do you want to teleport to?

And my responce:

-20

Aka: 20 stories down. :-/

For those who don't know, Nethack works on a "negative" scale.
Lvl 20 is 20 levels below. Lvl -20 is 20 stories up, that is, above
the clouds.

Well, the rest... is history.

